1
00:00:02,665 --> 00:00:06,558
Compare countries on food, poverty, health and education,

2
00:00:06,558 --> 00:00:09,427
and check every number against its source.

3
00:00:10,029 --> 00:00:11,156
Pick a country.

4
00:00:11,156 --> 00:00:16,644
Kenya's profile opens with 18 indicators from the UN System Data Commons,

5
00:00:16,644 --> 00:00:21,379
each with its latest value, its year, and its trend since 2015.

6
00:00:21,981 --> 00:00:23,608
At the top, plain findings.

7
00:00:23,608 --> 00:00:25,778
On the left, the country on its own:

8
00:00:25,778 --> 00:00:29,152
what improved, what worsened, and where data is missing.

9
00:00:29,152 --> 00:00:33,431
On the right, how it compares with the countries or regions you choose.

10
00:00:34,031 --> 00:00:35,212
Add a comparator.

11
00:00:35,212 --> 00:00:39,451
A country, a UN region, or a custom group you build yourself.

12
00:00:40,053 --> 00:00:44,434
The Baseline view sets every indicator against the median country.

13
00:00:44,434 --> 00:00:47,553
There is no overall score, and no league table.

14
00:00:48,155 --> 00:00:50,091
Compare shows the gap in bars,

15
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:53,125
and where the country sits among all countries.

16
00:00:53,727 --> 00:00:56,137
Trend shows change over time,

17
00:00:56,137 --> 00:00:59,877
against the 2015 baseline and the SDG target.

18
00:01:00,479 --> 00:01:03,908
The map shows the world as a globe, or as a flat map.

19
00:01:03,908 --> 00:01:05,914
Drag the globe, switch to flat,

20
00:01:05,914 --> 00:01:08,179
and click any country to select it.

21
00:01:09,581 --> 00:01:11,298
Every value can be checked.

22
00:01:11,298 --> 00:01:15,812
This table shows the value in the platform, the official current value,

23
00:01:15,812 --> 00:01:18,801
the reporting agency, and a link to the source.

24
00:01:19,404 --> 00:01:23,352
Some official values are thresholds, not measurements.

25
00:01:23,352 --> 00:01:26,715
Undernourishment below 2.5% is shown that way,

26
00:01:26,715 --> 00:01:29,054
and never used to compute a gap.

27
00:01:29,657 --> 00:01:34,652
We compared all 48,089 observations with the official publisher.

28
00:01:34,652 --> 00:01:38,477
94% are identical, and every difference is shown.

29
00:01:39,079 --> 00:01:42,568
It works in the six UN languages, including Arabic,

30
00:01:42,568 --> 00:01:43,799
in light and dark.
